# ZAPI Collections — Static SPA (Browser)

**Load the catalog first:** `zapi-developer-catalog.mdc` — `GET /api/v1/developer/catalog` (or `~/api/src/zapi/developer/app_services.manifest.json`).

Static apps call **ZAPI** at `VITE_VTC_API_URL` (typically `https://api.vtc.com/api/v1`) with `Authorization: Bearer` JWT. Use `src/lib/vtcApi.ts` (`vtcFetch`, `vtcAuthHeaders`) and the protected helpers `src/lib/vtcDocuments.ts`, `src/lib/vtcPaths.ts`.

**Do not** use legacy Platform API paths (`/collections/{name}/list|create|update|delete`) or Mongo-style query bodies.

## Document shape

ZAPI stores each record as:

```json
{
  "_id": "6a4d23c741b6804761f45df1",
  "data": {
    "title": "My palette",
    "created_by": "1",
    "group_id": "1",
    "status": "active",
    "created_at": "2026-07-07T16:00:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-07T16:00:00Z"
  }
}
```

- Business fields live inside **`data`**, using **snake_case** — see `data-model.mdc` (`created_at`, `updated_at`, `created_by`, `group_id`).
- App-facing TypeScript types may use camelCase; **normalize** between API docs and UI types in collection helpers under `src/components/lib/`.
- Document id for routes and keys is **`_id`** from the API (expose as `id` in UI types if needed).

## List documents

```http
GET /collections/{collection}/documents?page=1&page_size=100
Authorization: Bearer {jwt}
```

Response:

```json
{
  "documents": [ { "_id": "...", "data": { } } ],
  "total": 1,
  "page": 1,
  "page_size": 100,
  "total_pages": 1
}
```

- `vtcFetch` URL = `getVtcApiBase()` + path — **path must not include `/api/v1`** (base already ends with it). Use `vtcCollectionPath()` for collection paths.

## Get one document

```http
GET /collections/{collection}/documents/{_id}
```

Use `getDocument(collection, id)`.

## Create document

```http
POST /collections/{collection}/documents
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": { "title": "...", "created_by": "1", "status": "active", "created_at": "...", "updated_at": "..." } }
```

Use `createDocument(collection, dataFields)` — it wraps `{ data }` for you.

## Update document

```http
PUT /collections/{collection}/documents/{_id}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": { "title": "...", "updated_at": "..." } }
```

Use `updateDocument(collection, id, dataFields)`. Soft delete: `updateDocument(..., { status: 'deleted', updated_at })`.

## Forbidden patterns

| Pattern | Why |
|---------|-----|
| `PUT /collections/.../documents/query` | **Not a query endpoint** — ZAPI treats `query` as a document id → validation errors |
| `POST/PUT` body `{ filter, sort, limit }` without `data` | Mongo query DSL — not ZAPI |
| Flat `POST` body `{ title, ... }` without `data` wrapper | Missing required `data` field |
| camelCase in `data` (`createdAt`, `creatorId`) | Prefer snake_case per `data-model.mdc` |

## Shared app scoping

When `group_id !== '0'`, every list helper must filter to the active space:

```typescript
const filter = { group_id: user.group_id, status: { $ne: 'deleted' } } // logical filter in app code
```

Apply in collection helpers after `listAllDocuments()` — see `app-types.mdc`.

## Per-document ACL (ZAPI-enforced)

When a collection has document ACL enabled (space admin via `POST /collections/{name}/document-acl` with `{ "enabled": true }`), ZAPI filters list/get and guards update/delete server-side. Static Vite apps do **not** need `src/app/api/` for ACL — store ACL fields on each document and let ZAPI enforce.

**Document fields** (inside `data`, snake_case):

| Field | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `visibility` | `"network"` = all space members; omit or `"private"` = allowlist only |
| `created_by` | Creator `user_id` — auto-stamped on create |
| `allowedUserIds` | Specific people who may read |
| `allowedRoleIds` | Group-defined role IDs (`role.role_id`) |
| `allowedListIds` | Member list IDs — ZAPI checks caller's list memberships at read time |

**Admin bypass:** JWT `role_type` `"1"`/`"2"` sees all documents.

**Write policy:** Pair document ACL with `POST /collections/{name}/write-policy` `{ "policy": "creator_or_admin" }` for typical private-sharing apps.

**Builder:** On build/publish, Builder enables document ACL + `creator_or_admin` write policy for collections whose plan has `inAppAccess.visibility: private`.

**Public read:** `GET /public/collections/...` only returns documents with `visibility: network` when document ACL is enabled.

## Collection helpers (editable)

Codegen adds per-entity files under `src/components/lib/` (e.g. `paletteApi.ts`):

1. Import `listAllDocuments`, `getDocument`, `createDocument`, `updateDocument` from `../../lib/vtcDocuments`
2. `normalizeX(doc: ZapiDocument)` — map `_id` + `data` → app types
3. Never reimplement raw fetch shapes — extend the protected scaffold only

